[OPT_METAFILE]
\par -m, \--metafile=TOCFILE
Specify a ToC file for the original medium. Accepted formats are listed by
\b --list-toc-formats. The file must provide track offsets and may optionally
provide sample count and audio file names. Audio filename provided as separate
arguments override names from TOCFILE. Unreadable files cause the program to
exit with an error.
[OPT_METAFILE]

